## Backend structure

- Require `{{backend.root}}`, `{{backend.appsRoot}}`, and
  `{{backend.libsRoot}}` to be normalized target-relative paths without
  absolute roots, traversal, or unresolved values.
- Require the application and library roots to be distinct strict descendants
  of the backend root and reject duplicate or frontend/backend collisions.
- Require `{{backend.scopeName}}` to be one safe path segment.
- Keep maintained applications, reusable libraries, generated artifacts,
  infrastructure adapters, and domain code in explicit non-overlapping
  boundaries.
- A workspace provider is optional; the resolved backend paths remain valid
  when selected independently.
